<title>NETHERLANDS: AHOLD PLANS 3-FOR-1 SHARE SPLIT.</title>
<headline>AHOLD PLANS 3-FOR-1 SHARE SPLIT.</headline>
<dateline>ZAANDAM, Netherlands 1997-03-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Dutch supermarkets group Ahold NV said on Thursday it planned a three-for-one share split.</p>
<p>Ahold said it would ask shareholders to approve the split at their annual meeting on May 6, adding that it would then take effect on July 21.</p>
<p>Ahold said its shares currently had a nominal value of 1.25 guilders.</p>
<p>It said it planned to replace each of them with three shares of 0.50 guilders nominal value, raising its authorised share capital to account for the extra 0.25 guilders.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
